        <mxCell id="N5qRzYUOlFnT5I4Dg1us-1" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Data recorded while traversing on the roof in a snake pattern, on a random path, and not a pre-defined path.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The data were recorded with the position accuracy set to 1.5m and 0.9m on the RTK base in Survey-in configuration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The plots of both the recordings are below respectively. Since data were not recorded while traversing a pre-defined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;path, we can not compare or analyse much from these data. Also we could not see any sort of deviation from the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;track in both the data, they look very similar. We can repeat the recording in a sharply pre-defined path, so that we&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;compare the accuracy in the Rover&#39;s position more accurately.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
